eye-contact-co-processing-at-the-speed-of-light-lines-5 = cons "## 2. The Speed of Light: Physical Lower Bound on Latency" (cons "" (cons "Special relativity fixes the speed of light $c$ as the causal boundary of any light cone: no physical interaction can transmit information faster than electromagnetic propagation. In air ($n \approx 1.0003$), photons travel at approximately $2.997 \times 10^8\text{ m/s}$, crossing a two-meter conversational distance in roughly $6.7\text{ ns}$." (cons "" (cons "By comparison, acoustic speech propagates at $\approx 343\text{ m/s}$, taking $\approx 5.8\text{ ms}$ over the same two meters—over $870{,}000\times$ slower (`neuro/eye-contact.hypercubical`, `ec-light-beats-sound-ratio`). On neural integration timescales (tens to hundreds of milliseconds), optical transit between two people is effectively instantaneous. The physical channel operates at the relativistic lower bound on latency." (cons "" nil)))))
